 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Try using short clear lines, instead of long thin ones. Start each line at the same spot, around mid point. Then start each line at the same spot. It looks like a simple drawing, but it's really alive. Try drawing over someone else's rough sketch. It' great way to get fast feedback. Not really. Most people appreciate the effort. You' be surprised how much a simple change in line length and start point makes. Try it on something simple, like a drawing of your house",
